00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.950
<i>The Asakusa Expedition Series:</i>

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:09.310
<b>When the form resembles a 
living creature, it comes across
 as kind of monstrous and scary</b>

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:09.480
<b>The mechanical-type's strengths are clear
from it's speed and horsepower. Uses weapons primarily
in battle, but also has a force field.
 A bad fit for school!</b>

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:09.520
"Speculating on the Whole Body 
Based on the Footprint."

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:09.520
<b>Trapezoid
 aperture.</b>

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.520
<b>Sword</b>

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.520
m 476 215 l 479 342 626 342 612 212

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.520
<b>The slacks-type is a robot with a natural outline, and it's hard
 to predict its capabilities. 
It's kind of scary so I 
wouldn't want it showing up 
at school!

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.520
<b>Has lots of
 jetpacks</b>

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:09.520
<b>Joints snap shut like a jaw.</b>

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:19.530
The robot!

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:23.770
Something about how plain it looks 
makes it more realistic, and scary.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:27.450
Like, it'd barely be able to walk. It's so blocky!

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.300
And it's got an action camera for an eye!

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.710
Weapons development is behind schedule.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:33.670
Kanamori?!

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.650
Would this really be able to kill them?

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.490
We're not bloodthirsty. 
Suppression is good enough.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:40.260
So...

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:42.450
No weapons, then?

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:43.470
Mizusaki!

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:47.580
She's been brainwashed... 
I can't believe they got her!

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.390
It's now clear that 66% 
of the Eizouken's members

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.480
are involved with this giant robot!

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.590
But wait... the way things are going,

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.990
the two of them being bad 
guys could be a red herring,

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.490
when in reality, I'm the real 
bad guy! And I have amnesia!

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.490
It can shoot a rocket from its arm.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.490
Nice. Can you fire it?

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:10.250
No, not here. It'd be too dangerous.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.270
Hey, it hit somebody!

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:17.630
Wait, Asakusa?

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.920
Aw, shoot! Someone get a towel!

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.700
As usual, she has incredible timing.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.180
What the heck is that thing?

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.800
This is Talos.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:31.150
A giant model robot that's been passed 
down through the robot club's history,

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.150
and although it's undergone modifications,
 it dates back over 100 years!

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:38.930
The robot club's roots can be 
traced back to the late 1800s,

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.820
before anyone knew what a "robot" was,

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.100
with a collection of individuals 
who studied French culture,

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.920
and were fascinated with "The Future Eve."

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:52.850
With the dawn of the 1900s, Japan created
 Asia's first robot, Gakutensoku,

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:55.630
which led to a shift in the 
group's focus to giant robots.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:59.350
And after basing their first model 
on the robot from 1952's

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:02.260
<i>The King and the Mockingbird</i>, 
it's continued to be modified...

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.430
To this very day!

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.510
They've just been changing the head—

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.510
Don't!

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.100
What are you two doing here, anyway?

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:15.560
They're hiring us to make an 
anime based on this robot.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.790
Robot! Anime! Fun...

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.900
Wait, what's the catch?

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.010
If nothing else, we'll be getting paid.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.410
You're such a money-grubber!

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.100
Bam!

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:28.490
You accept money in order to 
accept responsibility for a job!

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:33.250
Pay exists to ensure a 
quality standard for labor.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.700
If we're accepting money for this job,

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:38.370
it means we have an obligation 
to deliver to a certain standard.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.330
Which sounds more wholesome:

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.340
accepting money for something 
and being responsible for it,

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.310
or not getting paid and not 
caring how it turns out?

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.360
Yeah, but wouldn't not 
having to worry about money

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:50.020
and just making anime be the best?

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.210
I was thinking that!

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.980
Absolutely not!

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.700
It's 3.5 meters in height,

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:59.170
weighs 4.7 tons, and can
 move at up to 70 km/h...

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.310
That's fast... Wait, this thing can run?!

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:04.250
Nah, that ain't happening. 
It's got no power source.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.610
It says they want it to fight a giant monster.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.450
I don't see how it can be <i>all that</i> giant.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.390
I mean... three meters is pretty big!

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:14.500
Building-sized giant monsters are unrealistic!

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.930
I dunno about buildings, but a 
giraffe is taller than this thing.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.360
If the monster is only three meters tall,

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.380
wouldn't a heavy machine gun do the job?

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.330
Shooting in the middle of 
the city is too dangerous,

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:24.760
so they need the robot to take it down!

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.210
Wouldn't ramming it with a truck be easier?

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.750
It says that the monster has a heat attack.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:31.750
Okay, now <i>that</i> is unrealistic!

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.030
Maybe a fire-breathing giraffe...

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.770
I'd like to get a broad estimate on the budget,

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.570
No, it could be a rhino that threatens 
to burn the whole city down.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:39.270
so I can break down the time frame 
and the work hours involved.

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:36.800
Like how the Asian bombardier beetle can

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.580
emit a gas that's over 100 degrees Celsius.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.270
Seriously?

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.340
You'd need a machine gun for sure.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.730
Y'know, "massive frontal profile"

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.780
It'll also help with my analysis, 
which is already under way,

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:45.300
is basically giant humanoid 
robots in a nutshell.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.260
and knowing exactly how much 
more I need to figure out.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.210
Having an opening in the front 
would be like an exposed weakness,

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:50.330
so wouldn't it make more sense 
for the hatch to be on the back?

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:50.330
These...

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.180
...girls...

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:51.770
...are...

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:54.940
...annoying!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.000
<b><i>Episode 5       An Iron Giant Appears!</i></b>

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.370
<b><i>Keep</i></b>

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:57.740
<b><i>Your</i></b>

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.290
<b><i>Hands</i></b>

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:02.670
<b><i>Off</i></b>

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:13.660
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:21.870
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.020
Is this it?

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.070
Seems like it.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:31.250
Man, it goes so far down!

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.730
This underground pit is supposed 
to predate the school's construction.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:36.980
Why, exactly?

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:40.910
They built it beforehand to make it easier
to maintain pipes and the like.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:42.980
This is absolutely the kind of 
place a creature would pop up!

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.380
Are you scared, Asakusa?

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:52.080
All right, let's start scouting the location 
for our robot-versus-monster battle!

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:53.690
But I don't like being scared!

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:56.790
You're the one who wanted to 
stage the battle down here.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.180
And we're already stuck.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:04.730
It's rusted shut.

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:06.630
I think I've got some oil...

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:11.880
Scared...

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.500
Well, it didn't open! Let's leave!

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.510
There's no such thing as 
a door that doesn't open.

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:18.070
A door's whole job is opening.

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:19.380
So do your damn job!

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:25.360
Classic Kanamori! She can even get 
inanimate objects to fall in line.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:28.190
Considering this isn't live action, 
is location scouting really necessary?

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.250
Experience makes a difference.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:33.340
For the record, I'm not here 
to play explorer with you two.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:34.700
It helps stoke...

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:38.080
the imagination.

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:44.170
Seems pretty... haunted down here, huh?

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.340
<b>Asakusa's Anti-Poltergeist Loadout</b>

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:59.790
Hey, it's those shoes for kids 
that light up when you walk!

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.810
We're looking for monsters, 
not ghosts! Get serious!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:08.530
Oh, I'm sorry! What else do 
you have in that bag, Asakusa?

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:09.480
I'm not saying!

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.600
Would you two please focus on this?

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:15.860
We're going to have the spotlight 
at the culture festival.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:17.740
You didn't mention that!

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:21.830
The theme this year is robots, so the
 robot club will be the big stars.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:26.660
We're doing a promotional video for them,
 which will be good for us, too.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:28.150
That's a pretty big spotlight!

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.710
I'd settle for a desk lamp.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:32.910
I've always preferred quiet places, 
away from the lights.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.760
I thought you were afraid of the dark.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:39.650
If you want people to appreciate your work, 
it needs to see the light of day.

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:42.190
Isn't that the exact opposite 
of what we're doing right now?!

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:46.790
And for the record, dark places 
don't bother me. Creepy ones do!

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:52.340
Those boards are gonna break! 
Walk along the walls!

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:53.850
It'll be fine.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.650
But they sound so dull. And soft.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:56.890
They're rotten!

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:58.660
If there's a big hole underneath, we'll be dead!

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:02.660
It looks like there's more space up ahead.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.820
Fantastic! This place is perfect!

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:08.550
You're taking pictures too, Mizusaki?

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:09.540
Of course I am!

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.150
There's background animation to consider,

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:13.710
and the setting influences the movement!

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.380
Like that beam that looks 
like it could collapse!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:28.910
What exactly are you doing?

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:30.540
Picturing the in-frame imagery, I bet.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.250
That looks an awful lot like screwing around.

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:34.650
Well, it kind of is.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.740
We're making something fun.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.610
It's better to get out in the world 
than stare at a blank sheet of paper.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:42.630
Locations like this feed your imagination.

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:45.250
The things you experience 
personally lead to originality.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:46.300
Do you follow?

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:50.120
Over your fear of the dark now?

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:56.430
I forgot until you reminded me.

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:57.880
Asakusa!

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.090
Come here for a sec!

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.220
Whatcha want?

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:03.660
I want the monster to blast out of here!

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:04.900
From water?

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:05.970
Yeah.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.370
From out of the mist it appears...

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.140
A giant pistol crabtle!

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:13.480
Is that the right size?

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.100
It's a giant monster with 
an arm like a pistol shrimp,

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
<b>A Turtle x Crab
 Monster That Has
 the Claw of a
 Pistol Shrimp!</b>

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
Weight:
 Height:
 Length:

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
Has no tail

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
Pistol Crabtle:
 Combines Crab and
 "tle" from turtle"

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
The shell's thickness can change
 over time. Used defensively, 
but also helps with thermoregulation.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
Crab liver

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
Crab intestines

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
Crab stomach

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
The crabtle has two arms and four legs.
 These legs are supporting a body
 that weighs over six tons.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
Crab vision:
Not particularly
good or bad

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.130
Legs are covered in scales

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:18.040
that resembles both a crab and a turtle.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:21.670
By locking its open claw, flexing, 
and then releasing the lock,

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:25.850
<b>Bam!</b>

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:25.850
<b>This part is flexible</b>

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:25.850
<b>Locks it's open claw, builds up it's strength,
 and releases the lock to slam it shut,
 causing a shockwave.

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:25.290
the claws snap shut with a ton of force,
 causing a powerful shock wave!

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.510
It likes to eat Japanese alders 
that grow in wetlands.

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:29.430
<b>Likes to eat Japanese alders that grow in wetlands</b>

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:29.430
<b>What it looks like when eating</b>

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:29.430
<b>Closes with over one ton of force,
 but its opening strength isn't remarkable. Like a crocodile's jaws.</b>

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:29.430
Omnivorous; will eat wood,
 aquatic plants, and algae.

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:29.430
Here it's eating water
 chestnuts. Will not eat
 them when they are 
still covered in spines.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.370
They're generally pretty docile,
 and in the old days,

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:42.760
<b>Their relatively docile nature meant
 that, in the old days, people who
 lived in the wetlands used them
 for trade and land development.</b>

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:35.670
they helped the people of the wetlands 
with trade and land development!

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.180
That sounds more like livestock.

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:40.730
It's endearing, though.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:47.630
Couldn't you turn it into roast crab 
with a flamethrower, even without a robot?

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:49.850
You're going to set the robot club off again.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:53.890
Asakusa, sometimes your focus on 
realism can be pretty harsh on fiction.

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:56.270
Facing it will be our robot!

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.090
What should its weapon be?

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:00.090
How about fighting with a chainsaw?

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:02.330
Do you know how much work 
those teeth are to draw?!

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:04.780
You can't tell them apart when 
it's spinning, so it's fine.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.030
The handle!

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:07.530
A recoil starter!

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:17.540
The pistol crab's special attack 
is the massive shock wave

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:22.550
generated when it unlocks 
 its claw after flexing!

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.930
That's kind of like a forehead flick.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.020
So the robot digs into the 
ground with the chainsaw...

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:32.680
And uses it to move faster!

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.400
That's really intense! It seems super strong!

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:38.960
Let's head back!

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:40.400
You're just scared, aren't you?!

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:42.610
Asakusa—

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:43.820
Hang on, don't push!

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:52.790
We fell!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.440
I noticed.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.650
This is why I said to walk along the walls!

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:59.070
We're lucky these leaves were here.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:01.590
And it's nice and warm.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:04.540
Let's calm down and call for―

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:04.540
No reception.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:08.850
This place was used to dump leaves.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:12.100
And it's warm because the 
leaves are fermenting!

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.700
Which means there's gas everywhere...

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:16.060
If we stay here for too long, we'll die!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.810
<b>Dead</b>

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:19.820
At times like this...

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.320
You take out your rope,

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:22.820
take a sock off,

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:25.320
put your Swiss army knife in the sock,

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.700
tie it to the rope, and throw it!

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.950
Take out your collapsible shovel,

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.400
pile up the leaves and dirt in one spot,

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:33.950
to get some height...

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:35.790
And escape!

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:36.830
Holy cow.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.460
That's just who she is.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:42.670
Now that we've got our 
suggestions for the setting,

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.010
it's time for a meeting with the robot club.

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.340
Did you get a haircut, Kanamori?

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.300
I did.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:51.950
Girls, this is our first paid job!

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:53.740
We'll need game faces on in there!

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:57.470
I didn't know you could be so motivational.

00:13:58.010 --> 00:13:59.530
She's awkward in conversations,

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:02.270
so she tries to sound quirky 
as an emotional defense.

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:03.740
Are you trying to make me more defensive?!

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:05.870
The deal is basically done already,

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.160
so the presentation should 
be a piece of cake.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:12.060
We won't try to sell them 
on our own suggestions,

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.410
but instead, choose one of 
their suggestions to work on,

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.990
all while nudging things in 
the direction we want to take.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:20.040
Do you think they'll get mad again?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.910
It's not an actual disagreement,

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:26.800
so as long as they think they're in charge,
 it'll be a pretty smooth process.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:32.430
But for the worst case scenario... 
It wouldn't hurt to have an advantage.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.660
I'll put my feelers out for blackmail bait.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.170
The eizouken is bad news!

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.420
They're nothing but trouble!

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:42.490
I heard them mention that nonsense 
about frontal profiles myself!

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:43.580
There goes Ono, again.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:47.400
Those girls don't even enjoy fictional robots!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.300
The entire reason we wanted this anime made

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:53.640
was to secure funding for our new giant robot!

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.500
Yeah, but—

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.500
And who are we partnered with?!

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:59.070
The kind of plebs that would make an 
anime about a robot losing to a tank!

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:02.290
Even though the entire point of giant 
robots is that they're a fantasy!

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:07.260
Here! This is the plan I've put together 
to keep the eizouken under control!

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:09.060
When did you have time to make this?

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:17.140
<b>Take Down the Eizouken</b>

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.700
We need to think seriously 
about one thing!

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:14.840
Our love for robots, which the 
eizouken could never understand!

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:17.930
And the beauty of that love, and our ideology!

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:21.100
At this rate, we're going to be 
responsible for a reprehensible anime,

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:24.500
with the eizouken cooking up 
something full of homing lasers

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.080
Excuse us...

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:24.500
Excuse us!

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:25.340
No response.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.310
and sudden power ups, instead of realism!

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:26.590
He is being loud.

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:27.310
Ono...

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:28.230
Wait, Ono!

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:31.070
Before you said the whole appeal 
of giant robots is the fantasy!

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:31.070
Excuse us.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.070
We're here.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.070
<b>Take Down the Eizouken</b>

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:35.050
Before that unrealistic nonsense gets made,

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:39.200
<b>Take Down the Eizouken</b>

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:38.610
we need to find some advantage 
over the eizouken!

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:46.210
Well, our client certainly 
doesn't seem to trust us.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:48.210
Forgive me...

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.820
Such a lack of faith.

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:52.470
There have been times when this sort of 
thing could get you executed, you know?

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:54.300
<b>Take Down the Eizouken</b>

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:56.850
I think I'll make a record 
of this, for future use.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.720
<b>Take Down the Eizouken</b>

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:57.720
<b>Take Down the Eizouken</b>

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:01.020
Kanamori is really good at negotiating.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.980
I don't know if that's what I'd call it.

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:09.820
Your tea.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:12.170
We've got our documents right here.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:12.990
Right...

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:16.510
Asakusa, you can show them the actual proposal.

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:17.910
Oh, right.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:21.410
The idea is for it to take place on 
the Shibahama High School campus.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:22.260
All right...

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:25.750
Next are the details on the giant monster.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
<b>A Turtle x Crab
 Monster That Has
 the Claw of a
 Pistol Shrimp!</b>

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
Weight:
 Height:
 Length:

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
Has no tail

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
Pistol Crabtle:
 Combines Crab and
 "tle" from turtle"

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
The shell's thickness can change over time. Is used defensively, but also helps with thermoregulation.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
Crab liver

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
Crab intestines

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
Crab stomach

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
The crabtle has two arms
 and four legs. These legs
 are supporting a body
 that weighs over six tons.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
Crab vision:
Not particularly
good or bad

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
Legs are covered in scales

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:40.890
View from above

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:27.350
Is that a turtle?

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:29.140
I-It's a crabtle.

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:33.000
From combining crab and turtle... crabtle.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.520
It can generate shock waves with 
its claws, and has a heat attack.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:39.470
Underwater, it can create 
cavitation by closing its claws,

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:40.890
which results in sonoluminescence,

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:44.050
the plasma from which reaches 
a temperature of 5000 degrees Kelvin...

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:45.980
And a pressure of 1000 millibars.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.560
W-Whoa, isn't that a little extreme?

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:51.990
It's an ability taken from pistol shrimps,
which live in the Atlantic Ocean.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:58.610
Since it's 507.3 times the size, 
its abilities increase proportionately.

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:01.080
The robot sticks the chainsaw on its right arm

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.710
into the ground in order to move at high speeds.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:05.300
This is great, Ono.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:07.150
Doesn't sound like there are 
any last minute power-ups,

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:08.370
but it's just fantastical enough that—

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:09.460
This is all wrong!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:11.990
It can't have a flashy weapon like a chainsaw!

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.340
And it sounds like there's too much action!

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:16.600
I thought the robot club's goal was 
preaching the merits of down-to-earth,

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.340
real robot aesthetics!

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:20.540
But real robots are more like...

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:21.740
Not what I meant!

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:24.070
The big ones! That people pilot!

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:24.850
Then...

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.850
Not that, either!

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:29.590
It has to be humanoid and piloted by someone!

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:30.860
And it fights!

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:35.360
<b>Seeing someone stump for such a
typical contradiction is disheartening.</b>

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:35.360
It needs to be realistic! Like in 
real life! A real-life giant robot!

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:38.870
Realistically speaking, I thought it 
was generally accepted that humanoid robots

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:42.480
exceeding a certain size 
have really limited uses.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:45.710
It's true that human-scale 
ones could do more jobs.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.670
They'd be more versatile, I guess.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.790
It's frustrating, really.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.050
Even when tanks stop being useful,

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.050
it won't mean bipedal robots being deployed.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:56.380
They'll probably just make stronger tanks.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.810
Yeah, realistically speaking, 
they'd probably evacuate the town

00:17:56.380 --> 00:18:00.850
<b>Glass
Bottles
Fragile</b>

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:00.850
and then bring out the tanks.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:04.690
People who want to make robots 
because of anime run into that fact

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:06.150
sooner or later...

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:09.870
But what we're after has always been 
the machines we've admired in movies,

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:12.190
manga, light novels, and anime.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.940
<b>Take Down the Eizouken</b>

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.940
So it's reality that doesn't 
care about humanoid robots.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:20.700
Come to think of it, there are 
fewer giant robot anime lately...

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.680
Should I have not brought that up?

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:23.290
Yep.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.350
I get it.

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:28.270
I know it's actually impossible!

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:31.710
I realize that... it's probably impossible.

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:35.330
But I still want to pilot a robot, okay?!

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:37.720
So much I could die! Damn it!

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:42.990
"Anything one man can imagine, 
another man can make real"?!

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:44.910
Screw whoever said that!

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.730
Even if it's possible, if it 
doesn't happen during my lifetime,

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:50.990
then that Wells guy sold me a bill of goods!

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.480
<b>What a huge
 pain in the neck.</b>

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:52.620
I can see it right now when I close my eyes...

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:55.020
<b>I wish I had blackmail material to speed this negotiation along.</b>

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:59.090
And when I try to think about it 
realistically, it becomes contradictory!

00:18:55.020 --> 00:19:03.530
<b>Take Down the Eizouken</b>

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:01.820
I hate how it puts me in this place
where all I can do is dream!

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:03.530
I hate it so damn much!

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:04.460
<i>I see now.</i>

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:10.530
<i>He's not making sense because he
can't visualize the finished product.</i>

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:11.580
<i>That makes him so anxious,</i>

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:15.050
<i>all he can manage is a passionate 
plea full of incoherent ranting.</i>

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:18.370
<i>If we present a calm response,</i>

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:21.300
<i>it should calm him down 
and make controlling them—</i>

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:24.160
I wanna travel to the fringes of space!

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.430
I cry in the bath every night 
about how big the universe is!

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:31.830
I try to do a Hadoken every night before bed!

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.560
<i>You two are crying now?</i>

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:37.150
I like to imagine I'm in a cockpit 
when I'm on the toilet...

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.090
Comrade!

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:44.160
<b>Sudden harmony</b>

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:43.530
I have huge problems with people who 
solve problems with emotional appeals.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.490
All right, let's modify this robot together!

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:52.400
You mentioned having the hatch 
in the front would be a weakness,

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.750
and moving it to the back would help, right?

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.510
In the name of high adventure,

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:59.300
we're going to keep it in the front, 
like your actual model Talos.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.130
Plus...

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:05.140
You can do a shot reverse shot 
with the pilot and robot.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.750
Like this...

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:11.430
Which makes for a really cool 
depiction of two pilots talking!

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.990
I'm not so sure.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:16.250
I think having it open up 
in front seems weaker, too.

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:19.440
But the back of a robot 
has to look cool, too!

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.120
Okay, then.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:23.450
In that case, we'll ditch the 
rule of cool on the hatch,

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.450
and go for a safer choice.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:27.940
She's got a tendency to only enjoy working

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:31.450
when there's some odd line 
of reasoning into it.

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:32.870
Right here.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.460
Let's make the entrance on the top.

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:36.460
That works.

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:38.460
Next up is the cockpit.

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:41.460
It's not a cockpit unless 
it looks like this!

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.240
Analog-style instruments.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:46.090
CRT monitors have good response time.

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:49.090
The main monitor seems to have 
a pretty wide range of vision.

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:51.850
Is the camera in the mono-eye 
really going to cut it?

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:52.940
Should we add more?

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:53.740
Cameras?

00:20:53.740 --> 00:20:54.800
Let's change it.

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:56.400
Let's change the model and add some.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.160
We'll add more, and different, cameras!

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.380
Copy that.

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:03.910
The kind of cameras and sensors that 
robots use are usually along these lines.

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:07.110
So if we combine them...

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:08.190
Cool!

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:08.760
Lame!

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:11.370
Okay, how about something like this?

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:12.630
Ta-dah!

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:15.370
It's got kind of a classic vibe.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:16.870
Time to activate!

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:28.770
Are all these switches 
actually helpful as controls?

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:31.430
It shows that the people making robot anime

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:33.980
ultimately put their faith in people!

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:35.840
I'm disengaging the break!

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:38.980
Starboard clear!

00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:41.230
Port side clear!

00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:43.480
All clear below!

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:46.330
We're rising up! Please brace yourselves!

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:47.990
Wasn't it standing already?

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:51.340
Time to go for it!

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.020
All at once?!

00:21:54.020 --> 00:21:55.420
Oh man, I forgot seat belts!

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:56.750
Those are important!

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:00.750
We'll partially engage the clutch, 
 and then make our way up!

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:06.110
That's a lot of Gs!

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:09.890
Time to straighten up!

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:23.150
It... It stood!

00:22:23.510 --> 00:22:25.650
I want a pile bunker!

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:26.820
Okay!

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:28.910
It'd be a good idea to change 
the body to match the face!

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:30.980
A hydraulic cutter! Snip!

00:22:30.980 --> 00:22:33.380
We've come this far, let's go harder!

00:22:33.380 --> 00:22:34.660
How about a drill?

00:22:35.290 --> 00:22:37.620
A boom-mounted cutting head!

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:39.230
Is it a hole-digging robot now?!

00:22:39.230 --> 00:22:40.040
This one, then!

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:42.880
Those bits are for wood!

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:44.610
Ah, you noticed.

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:47.870
You realize the robot club is a 
technical club, right? Of course I did!

00:22:47.870 --> 00:22:49.130
At least use one for metal!

00:22:51.060 --> 00:22:53.900
It's already got a chainsaw! 
We're gonna need more arms.

00:22:54.460 --> 00:22:57.570
Can you even animate something 
with all these add-ons?

00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:00.280
Why not just remove the legs and make it fly?

00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:02.670
That'd take the fun out of making it move!

00:23:02.670 --> 00:23:06.340
But... is it okay if we cover up the joints?

00:23:07.610 --> 00:23:08.610
It's done!

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:09.730
Holy cow!

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:11.710
It looks totally different.

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:16.370
Isn't it kinda... elaborate?

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:18.620
Are you sure you can animate this thing?

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:22.270
We ended up with a blue-collar robot!

00:23:22.270 --> 00:23:24.080
But what'll happen next?!

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Fluffy~</b>

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Gahaha!</b>

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Illustration by Eito Aika</b>

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Eito Aika</b>
